+    wrapper_code.past_planning_states) and its wrapper's state at that stage (wrapper_code.planned_state). Neither
+    its entry's declaration nor any of its lines is written. `planned` is those planned lines (wrapper_code.lines),
+    `const_planned` its const graph's (graph.const_module's, aot_inductor.use_runtime_constant_folding; None: no
+    const graph). emit(supplied, const_supplied) is one emission from that planned stage, for one configuration
+    (compile_fx's `emission`, under that stage's contexts): its const graph's wrapper emitted given `const_supplied`,
+    its code then its graph's; its own wrapper emitted given `supplied` (each wrapper set back to its planned state,
+    restore_planned, then resume_generation: its entry's declaration and its print, wrapper_code.supplied); then
+    AotCodeCompiler.compile's AotCompiled (torch-inductor-cpp-build-result.patch), which it returns. No emission
+    reruns the lowering or its plan, and its constants object is built by its first emission, each later one taking
+    that one's (AotCompiled.consts). `emitted` is each emission's (supplied, const_supplied, AotCompiled), in order.
